@startuml BillingSystemFlow
!theme plain
title LedgerGuard - Billing System Flow (Stripe + Trial-Freemium)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #94A3B8

|#E8F0FE|Firebase|
|#FFF3E0|Backend|
|#F3E5F5|Stripe|
|#E0F7FA|Flutter|
|#E8F5E9|n8n|

|Firebase|
start
:User signs up;

|Backend|
:Create user record\n(plan_tier = TRIAL\n(Starter-level trial));
:Create Stripe Customer\n(no payment method yet);
:Set trial_ends_at = NOW + 14 days;
:Insert billing_subscription\n(status = trialing);

|n8n|
:Send Welcome + Trial email\n(via Postmark);

|Flutter|
:Show trial banner\n""14 days remaining"";
:All features unlocked;

note right
  **Trial Period (14 days)**
  Day 7: email reminder
  Day 12: email reminder
  Day 13: in-app warning
end note

' === TRIAL EXPIRY ===

|Backend|
:Daily cron checks\ntrial_ends_at;

if (Trial expired?) then (yes)
  if (Payment method added?) then (yes)
    |Stripe|
    :Create Subscription\n(Stripe handles first invoice);
    :Fire checkout.session.completed;

    |Backend|
    :Update plan_tier = STARTER;
    :Update billing_subscription\n(status = active);

    |n8n|
    :Send ""Welcome to PRO"" email;

    |Flutter|
    :Remove trial banner;
    :All features remain unlocked;
  else (no)
    |Backend|
    :Update plan_tier = EXPIRED;
    :Update billing_subscription\n(status = free);

    |n8n|
    :Send ""Trial ended"" email\nwith upgrade CTA;

    |Flutter|
    :Show upgrade prompts;
    :Enter read-only mode;
    note right
      **Locked on FREE:**
      AI Chat
      API Keys
      Slack notifications
      Data export
      Multi-app (limit: 1)
    end note
  endif
else (no)
  :Continue trial;
endif

' === UPGRADE FLOW ===

|Flutter|
:User clicks ""Upgrade"";

|Backend|
:POST /api/v1/billing/checkout;
:Create Stripe Checkout Session;

|Stripe|
:Hosted Checkout Page;
:User enters payment method;
:Payment succeeds;
:Fire checkout.session.completed;

|Backend|
:POST /webhooks/stripe;
:Verify webhook signature;
:Check billing_events\nfor idempotency;
:Create billing_subscription\n(status = active, plan = PRO);
:Update user.plan_tier = PRO;

|Flutter|
:Redirect to success URL;
:Unlock STARTER features\n(or PRO if selected);

' === ONGOING BILLING ===

|Stripe|
:Monthly invoice generated;

if (Payment succeeds?) then (yes)
  :Fire invoice.paid;

  |Backend|
  :Renew subscription period;
  :Log billing_event;
else (no)
  :Fire invoice.payment_failed;

  |Backend|
  :Set status = past_due;
  :Send payment failed alert;

  |n8n|
  :Send ""Update payment"" email;

  |Stripe|
  :Retry payment (Stripe Smart Retries);
endif

' === CANCEL FLOW ===

|Flutter|
:User clicks ""Cancel Subscription"";

|Backend|
:POST /api/v1/billing/cancel;
:Stripe: cancel at period end;

|Stripe|
:User keeps PRO until period end;
:At period end fire\ncustomer.subscription.deleted;

|Backend|
:Set plan_tier = EXPIRED;
:Set billing_subscription\nstatus = canceled;

|Flutter|
:Enter read-only mode;
:Show ""Resubscribe"" option;

' === FEATURE GATING ===

|Backend|
:Request to protected endpoint\n(e.g. /api/v1/chat);
note right
  **Plan Middleware**
  1. Get user.plan_tier
  2. Check trial_ends_at
  3. Lookup plan_features
  4. Allow or 403
end note

if (Feature allowed for plan?) then (yes)
  :Process request normally;
else (no)
  :Return 403\n{error: ""upgrade_required"",\nplan: ""PRO"", feature: ""ai_chat""};

  |Flutter|
  :Show upgrade dialog\nwith plan comparison;
endif

stop

@enduml

' ============================================================================
' PAYMENT MONEY FLOW (Separate Diagram)
' ============================================================================
@startuml PaymentMoneyFlow
!theme plain
title LedgerGuard - Payment Money Flow (USD → Stripe → Developer Bank)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #10B981
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F0FDF4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #6EE7B7

|#E0F7FA|Customer|
|#F3E5F5|Stripe|
|#FFF3E0|Developer Bank|

|Customer|
start
:Customer subscribes\n$29.00/mo (Pro Monthly);
:Enter card details\non Stripe Checkout;

|Stripe|
:Process card payment\nGross: **$29.00**;
:Deduct Stripe fees\n~2.9% + $0.30 = **$1.14**;
:Net after fees: **$27.86**;

note right
  **Stripe Fee Breakdown**
  Processing: 2.9% × $29.00 = $0.84
  Fixed fee: $0.30
  Total: **$1.14**
  Net: $29.00 − $1.14 = **$27.86**
end note

if (Stripe India entity?) then (yes)
  :Convert USD → INR\nat market exchange rate;
  :Apply forex markup\n(~1-2% spread);
  note right
    **Example Conversion**
    $27.86 × ₹83.30 = ~**₹2,321**
    (rate varies daily)
  end note
else (no)
  :Hold in USD balance;
endif

:Queue for payout;

note right
  **Payout Schedule**
  Standard: **T+2** business days
  First payout: **T+7** business days
  Payout frequency: Daily (configurable)
end note

|Developer Bank|
:Receive bank deposit;
:Amount: **₹2,321** (INR)\nor **$27.86** (USD);

note right
  **Monthly Revenue Example**
  50 Pro subscribers × $29.00 = $1,450.00 gross
  Stripe fees: ~$57.00
  Net payout: ~$1,393.00
  INR equivalent: ~₹116,037
end note

stop

@enduml

' ============================================================================
' STRIPE CUSTOMER CREATION STRATEGIES (Separate Diagram)
' ============================================================================
@startuml StripeCustomerCreation
!theme plain
title LedgerGuard - Stripe Customer Creation Strategies

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #8B5CF6
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F3FF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #A78BFA

start

:User registers\n(Firebase Auth);

if (When to create\nStripe Customer?) then

  ' Option A - CHOSEN
  :====\n**Option A: At Signup [CHOSEN]**\n====;
  note right #E0F7FA
    **Why Option A was chosen:**
    1. Simplifies trial tracking
       (Stripe Customer exists from day 1)
    2. Stripe can send trial reminder emails
       (customer.subscription.trial_will_end)
    3. No lazy-init complexity
    4. Associates user with Stripe immediately
    5. Enables Stripe Customer Portal access
       even during trial
    6. Industry standard for SaaS
  end note

  :Create Stripe Customer\nimmediately on signup;
  :Store stripe_customer_id\nin billing_subscriptions;
  :No payment method yet;
  :Start 14-day trial;

  note left
    **Stripe Customer at Signup**
    stripe.customers.create({
      email: user.email,
      name: user.name,
      metadata: {
        user_id: user.id,
        source: "signup"
      }
    })
  end note

elseif (Option B) then

  :====\n**Option B: At First Checkout**\n====;
  note right #FFF3E0
    **Trade-offs:**
    + Fewer Stripe Customers created
      (only paying users)
    + Lower Stripe API calls
    - Cannot use Stripe trial features
    - Must build own trial tracking
    - More complex checkout flow
      (create customer + subscription)
    - No Stripe Customer Portal
      during trial
  end note

  :Trial runs without Stripe;
  :Create Stripe Customer\nonly when user subscribes;
  :Combine with Checkout Session;

elseif (Option C) then

  :====\n**Option C: At Trial End**\n====;
  note right #FEF3C7
    **Trade-offs:**
    + Fewest Stripe Customers
    + No Stripe involvement during trial
    - Cannot use Stripe trial reminders
    - Delayed Stripe integration
    - Risk: user leaves before
      Stripe Customer created
    - No pre-trial payment method
      collection
  end note

  :Trial runs independently;
  :At trial expiry, prompt user;
  :Create Stripe Customer\nonly if user decides to pay;

endif

stop

@enduml
